    title: "Rare look at the remote engine rooms fuelling China's AI boom",
    summary: "The BBC is in Inner Mongolia where dozen of Chinese data centres are being constructed, as the country aims to lead the world in artificial intelligence.",
    preview: "The BBC's Laura Bicker is in Inner Mongolia where dozens of Chinese data centres are being built, as the country aims to lead the world in artificial intelligence. She explains how attitudes differ between people in China and the US when it comes to the data centre industry, ahead of leaders Xi Jinping and Donald Trump's meeting in Washington later this week. Related topics - China-US relationsUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
